my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
line one
line two
line three
line four
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{u restores cursor position after dd},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_cursor_position`

Tests that **u** not only restores the deleted line content but also
restores the cursor to its original position (line and column).

**Keys:** `j`, `l`, `dd`, `u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 4 lines: "line one", "line two", "line three", "line four"
- Cursor on line 2, column 1 (on 'i' of "line two")

**after_dd.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "line one", "line three", "line four"
- "line two" was deleted
- Cursor moved to line 2 (now "line three")
- Intermediate snapshot showing the deletion

**after_undo_cursor_restored.png**
- Buffer restored to 4 lines (identical to initial)
- Cursor back on line 2, column 1 (original position restored)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('jl');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo_cursor_restored');
    },
}
